{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/978770-abilities-beyond-5","id":978770,"title":"Abilities beyond 5?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-29T18:43:14-07:00","id":978770,"title":"Abilities beyond 5?","content":"So, there are systems in place for characters who wish to go beyond 5 dots in attributes. (Enhancement, Permanent Life... with permadox and genetic flaws and all that).<br /> <br /> Is there a similar system for Abilities?<br /> <br /> I can certainly imagine effects running the range from straight Mind, to combo effects including Life and mind to develop &quot;muscle memory&quot; or Matter and Mind to transfer a text into a usable Knowledge... Or time and Mind to learn stuff quickly... whatever fits the ole paradigm/practice... <br /> <br /> My main concern isn't with increasing those dots past 5... it's a question of how much strain would breaking that dot 5 barrier put on the pattern in terms of permadox or genetic flaws... <br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12296-gabryl","name":"Gabryl","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T22:11:52-07:00","id":978855,"title":"","content":"I always tend to think of '5' as the maximum for beginning characters and '8' to be the true maximum for human potential. In order to go above '5' without magic, I usually required people to spend twice as much experience points as normal. Using magic, I usually required one point of permanent Paradox per dot of permanent Attribute/Ability increase, not just over '5', for game balance purposes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T22:49:05-07:00","id":978872,"title":"","content":"I take another approach:<br /> 1. Points over 5 = Permadox<br /> 2. Paid for it with XP or he gets pattern bleeding.<br /> 3. Pattern bleeding being one quint or if no quint is available 1 level of agg.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T14:59:57-07:00","id":979276,"title":"","content":"There's no official support for this sort of thing for Mages (vampires and Exalts of all stripes can reach Ability 6+ with high Essence/low Generation, of course). I could quite easily see a Merit to parallel Legendary Attribute, or use of Mind 4 to imprint Abilities beyond normal human maximums. Maybe a 3-pointer given the relatively constrained applicability Abilities have compared to Attributes. Or soul trading for Ability Investments up to similar limits as Attributes i.e. 8.<br /> <br /> Naturally, like in all things, going beyond normal limits without use of static magic will incur some Permanent Paradox. I'd probably peg it as 1 'dox per two Ability points, rounded up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","name":"Quantumboost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6072_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"590"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T15:32:06-07:00","id":979293,"title":"","content":"Well, if it can help, there's an entry in VtM (Revised) where mages can have occult 6, which is the minimum necessary to reverse the embrace. It doesn't say anything else, only that it's rare and, nothing about permadox.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T12:42:32-07:00","id":980949,"title":"","content":"I think for Abilities I'd be inclined to let mages buy past 5 dots only if they've lived beyond a normal human lifespan and devoted a significant amount of that time to mastering the Ability in question. But since it's learned skills or expertise rather than something more tangible I wouldn't apply permanent Paradox to it like I would for, say, 6+ dots of Str or Dex.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T14:48:14-07:00","id":981035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/978770-abilities-beyond-5?p=978855#post978855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always tend to think of '5' as the maximum for beginning characters and '8' to be the true maximum for human potential. In order to go above '5' without magic, I usually required people to spend twice as much experience points as normal. Using magic, I usually required one point of permanent Paradox per dot of permanent Attribute/Ability increase, not just over '5', for game balance purposes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Quite odd. You go for it with XP and it's paradox free, or you suffer paradox if you use Magick ? I cannot understand that. Paradox happens when Consensus cannot accept it as real. There are two possibilities here in my opinion:<br /> - Either it's not acceptable for the Consensus and then you can use magick to enhance your abilities beyond 5 and get permadox for it,<br /> - Or Reality can accept it and you can pay for it with XP in a mundane way, but if you chose to make that possible, doing it with magick should not induce paradox.<br /> <br /> After all, if you can go for it with mundane skill, it is acceptable for Reality by definition and should not create paradox if you do it with magick. What do you think ?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/978770-abilities-beyond-5?p=978872#post978872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I take another approach:<br /> 1. Points over 5 = Permadox<br /> 2. Paid for it with XP or he gets pattern bleeding.<br /> 3. Pattern bleeding being one quint or if no quint is available 1 level of agg.</div> </div> </div> </div>What is your base time period for this bleeding ? Do you require a quintessence spent each week ? Each month ? For attributes, HDYDT states that it should cost 1lvl of lethal every day until the payment is due. Either way, it costs half the XP if it is done with Magick (when it's a permanent spell of course).<br /> <br /> In all cases, you would get permanent paradox. Myself, if it is not too vulgar, I would tend to limit pattern bleeding to Mages with permanent paradox going beyond 3 dots. Well, surely you can tank some permanent pardox don't you think ? It's costly enough at the begining... But the situation never happened to my players, so I cannot be sure of how I would react.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","name":"NicoTheDuck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T15:13:46-07:00","id":981056,"title":"","content":"It depends on the scarcity of quint in the chronicle.<br /> <br /> If you have access to a Node rank 3 and 3 Permadox the pattern bleeding leaves you with 1 quint left.<br /> <br /> To date no player in my groups made any stat boosting enhancements permanent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T16:09:58-07:00","id":981086,"title":"","content":"I never let players get any Trait for free from using magick. If they increase any Trait with magick beyond 24 hours, they get one point of permanent Paradox per dot of increase, whether they are going from 1 to 2 or 5 to 10. It is simply a matter of game balance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T00:37:18-07:00","id":981317,"title":"","content":"My Players get Permadox as soon as something goes above 5, even if it is only for a scene.<br /> <br /> The Permadox is staying as long as the origin of it persists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T13:30:06-07:00","id":981658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NicoTheDuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/978770-abilities-beyond-5?p=981035#post981035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quite odd. You go for it with XP and it's paradox free, or you suffer paradox if you use Magick ? I cannot understand that. Paradox happens when Consensus cannot accept it as real. There are two possibilities here in my opinion:<br /> - Either it's not acceptable for the Consensus and then you can use magick to enhance your abilities beyond 5 and get permadox for it,<br /> - Or Reality can accept it and you can pay for it with XP in a mundane way, but if you chose to make that possible, doing it with magick should not induce paradox.<br /> <br /> After all, if you can go for it with mundane skill, it is acceptable for Reality by definition and should not create paradox if you do it with magick. What do you think ?</div> </div> </div> </div>There are... some parallels for doing it via 'mundane' means not giving Permanent Paradox. Or perhaps I should say 'static' means.<br /> <br /> For instance, Legendary Attribute is a Merit, and there's nothing <i>strictly</i> preventing a Sleeper or Sorcerer from taking it in the merit itself IIRC. It's 'static magic', in much the way that having say Green Thumb or Parlor Trick is. In my mind, that essentially means that because of your circumstances or your person, <i>something</i> causes the Consensus to 'accept' you having superhuman Attributes and special abilities when Dynamically increasing them would give you Permadox. Hercules has superhuman Strength, and reality is like &quot;sure why not&quot;.<br /> <br /> Given the experience costs involved, raising it that way might be excused in Consensus by essentially pulling Mythic Threads/memes based on &quot;Training from Hell&quot; into letting you expand beyond 'normal' limits. A Mage who raises them without undergoing that additional cost hasn't &quot;put in the hours&quot; and reality won't cut them a break.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","name":"Quantumboost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6072_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"590"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T06:39:38-07:00","id":982096,"title":"","content":"Yes, it is using experience points (or freebie points) rather than magick that preserves game balance (there are plenty of ways to exceed '5' without gaining permanent Paradox, such as becoming a fomori or entering into an Infernal Pact). Legendary Attribute is actually more useful for the bonus power than allowing Attributes to reach '6'. For example, Legendary Stamina allows you to soak any damage, from any source, as if the damage were bashing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T11:53:48-07:00","id":982243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/978770-abilities-beyond-5?p=981086#post981086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never let players get any Trait for free from using magick. If they increase any Trait with magick beyond 24 hours, they get one point of permanent Paradox per dot of increase, whether they are going from 1 to 2 or 5 to 10. It is simply a matter of game balance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your rule is very constraining. Everyone can grow a point of characteristic at one point if it remains in the bounds of Consensus. Growing characteristics should not even be vulgar. Well, I will play it vulgar if one of my player wants to go from 1 dot to 5 dots in a characteristic in one turn, or go beyond 5. However, just increasing characteristics is not vulgar. So getting a permadox for that seems harsh to me. Or are you the kind of ST that states that everything is vulgar ? I know some poeple play Mage that way. Omniscient witness something it is called if I do not mistake. If it is the case, then it is consistent so ok. But if not, It seems very restrictive to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","name":"NicoTheDuck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T13:01:49-07:00","id":982283,"title":"","content":"Temporary increases are fine as long as they do not last longer than 24 hours. If players want to increase a trait for more than 24 hours, they are required to spend something (XP, temporary autonomy, soul points, etc) to avoid permanent Paradox. It is a game balance issue. Otherwise, mages who invest in Life and Mind can just permanently increase all of their attributes to 5 without paying any XP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T13:11:46-07:00","id":982295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/978770-abilities-beyond-5?p=982283#post982283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Temporary increases are fine as long as they do not last longer than 24 hours. If players want to increase a trait for more than 24 hours, they are required to spend something (XP, temporary autonomy, soul points, etc) to avoid permanent Paradox. It is a game balance issue. Otherwise, mages who invest in Life and Mind can just permanently increase all of their attributes to 5 without paying any XP.</div> </div> </div> </div>The existing rules are already balanced. Your house rule may suit your needs more specifically, but presenting the necessity for them as a matter of game balance.<br /> <br /> Also, I seem to recall that in order to permanently increase attributes with magic you still have to spend half XP, not &quot;without paying any xp&quot; at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T13:21:37-07:00","id":982303,"title":"","content":"No, I do not think that those rules are balanced, but everyone will play the game their own way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T23:44:18-07:00","id":982578,"title":"","content":"I ran a Mage chronicle for like four years. Not the longest ever, but definitely not short. I never found the rules to be particularly unbalanced.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T21:09:53-07:00","id":984225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/978770-abilities-beyond-5?p=981056#post981056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It depends on the scarcity of quint in the chronicle.<br /> <br /> If you have access to a Node rank 3 and 3 Permadox the pattern bleeding leaves you with 1 quint left.<br /> <br /> To date no player in my groups made any stat boosting enhancements permanent.</div> </div> </div> </div>This depends on how much Quintessence each dot of Node can give. I can't speak for all editions, but M20 leaves it up to the Storyteller, and I vaguely remember Revised saying the same. If your rank 3 Node gives very little Quint, this above is true. But if it gives 5 or more per dot, it's much less of an issue.<br /> <br /> But yes, it's a matter of how scare the Quint is, by Storyteller fiat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T23:46:04-07:00","id":984285,"title":"","content":"Regardless how much quint a node gives, if you have 3 Permadox worth of pattern bleeding and a rank 3 node then the pattern bleeding consumes all but 1 of the quint the node delivers (x-(x-1)=1)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T16:37:40-07:00","id":986464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/978770-abilities-beyond-5?p=982578#post982578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I ran a Mage chronicle for like four years. Not the longest ever, but definitely not short. I never found the rules to be particularly unbalanced.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It may also be due to different play experiences. Did you have one player paying full XP for all of their attribute purchases with another paying half XP? I can see that causing some ugliness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T17:53:53-07:00","id":986496,"title":"","content":"Or any Trait. Trait discounts are always unbalanced because players will always seek to exploit their discount.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T20:52:13-07:00","id":986559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tytalus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/978770-abilities-beyond-5?p=986464#post986464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It may also be due to different play experiences. Did you have one player paying full XP for all of their attribute purchases with another paying half XP? I can see that causing some ugliness.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, had a couple of players paying half xp and a few paying full. No one complained to me about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T20:56:48-07:00","id":986562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gabryl</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/978770-abilities-beyond-5#post978770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, there are systems in place for characters who wish to go beyond 5 dots in attributes. (Enhancement, Permanent Life... with permadox and genetic flaws and all that).<br /> <br /> Is there a similar system for Abilities?<br /> <br /> I can certainly imagine effects running the range from straight Mind, to combo effects including Life and mind to develop &quot;muscle memory&quot; or Matter and Mind to transfer a text into a usable Knowledge... Or time and Mind to learn stuff quickly... whatever fits the ole paradigm/practice...<br /> <br /> My main concern isn't with increasing those dots past 5... it's a question of how much strain would breaking that dot 5 barrier put on the pattern in terms of permadox or genetic flaws...<br /> <br /> Thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I just made Arete the limit for Attributes and abilities both.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T21:55:06-07:00","id":986577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/978770-abilities-beyond-5?p=986559#post986559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, had a couple of players paying half xp and a few paying full. No one complained to me about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow - that wouldn't fly in any group I played with. Once again - &quot;house rules&quot; don't fit all houses. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T22:11:42-07:00","id":986583,"title":"","content":"Never had even one problem neither on that matter. For one, you still have to get half the xp and the necessary spheres. Anyway, my players often prefer to level up abilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","name":"NicoTheDuck","avatar":"d